          {
            title: 'Crazy Eights',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: United States\nTime Period: 1930s\nCreator(s): Unknown (folk game)\nEtymology: Named after the wild 8 cards that can "go crazy" and change suits',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 7\nOptimal Players: 3-5\nPartnerships: No (individual play)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included (optional in some variations)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck of playing cards\nFlat surface for discard pile',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Players  Cards per Player \n---------------------------\n 2 players  7 cards each \n 3-4 players  5 cards each \n 5-7 players  5 cards each \nDealing Pattern: Clockwise, one card at a time\nIf the turned-up card is an 8, it is buried in the middle of the pack and the next card is turned up\n--',
              },
            ],
